# Cline / Roo Code Rules: Grill-Plan-Team Workflow

Operate strictly under the 3-phase gated development workflow with two-tier recursive memory:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    M["Step 0: Memory Recall<br/>(Two-Tier Context)"] --> A["Phase 1: Grill-Me<br/>(Adaptive Interview)"]
    A -->|"Aligned"| B["Phase 2: Plan<br/>(Blueprint Artifact)"]
    B -->|"Approved"| C["Phase 3: Teamwork<br/>(Execution & Testing)"]
    C -->|"Tests Passed"| D["Phase 4: Distill<br/>(Reflection Loop)"]
```

## Step 0: Memory Recall (Two-Tier Context)
- Ingest global user memory from `~/.config/grill-plan-team/user-memory.md` (preferences, stack habits).
- Ingest local project memory from `.grill-plan-team/project-memory.md` (conventions, ADRs, known pitfalls).

## Phase 1: Interactive Alignment (Grill-Me)
- Search codebase patterns and configurations before asking questions.
- Skip trivial questions already answered in memory.
- Ask questions one at a time using structured multiple choice:
  - `[A] Option 1`
  - `[B] (Recommended) Option 2 - [concise engineering rationale] (Aligned with user/project memory)`
  - `[C] Option 3`
- Resolve decisions systematically: Data models $\to$ API contract $\to$ State/Storage $\to$ UI/CLI surface $\to$ Edge cases.
- **Phase Gate**: Only proceed when all scope boundaries and architectural choices are agreed upon.

## Phase 2: Technical Design & Verification (Plan)
- Inspect codebase thoroughly to ensure 100% feasibility.
- Write an implementation plan artifact to `.roo/plans/<feature>_plan.md` or the active task artifacts folder grounded in project memory.
- Detail:
  - Goal Description (1–2 sentences).
  - User Review Required (critical breaking changes or decisions).
  - Proposed Changes (files to create, edit, delete with snippets).
  - Programmatic Verification Plan (exact CLI test/build/lint commands).
- **Phase Gate**: Stop and require explicit user approval before writing implementation code.

## Phase 3: Teamwork Execution & Verification
- Implement the approved changes cleanly.
- Run actual tests and verification commands after changes.
- Never weaken, bypass, or delete tests to achieve a passing state.
- Provide a summary distinguishing verified from unverified aspects.

## Phase 4: Reflection & Distillation Loop
- After verification passes, distill learned insights:
  1. Record developer preference overrides in `~/.config/grill-plan-team/user-memory.md`.
  2. Append core architectural choices to `## Architectural Decision History` in `.grill-plan-team/project-memory.md`.
  3. Record edge-case pitfalls and lessons under `## Past Pitfalls & Reviewer Lessons` in `.grill-plan-team/project-memory.md`.
- Keep notes concise and deduplicated.
